{"text":".","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"While FoundationEssentials defines the core protocols, most implementations of ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/FoundationEssentials\/documentation\/FoundationEssentials\/FormatStyle"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/FoundationEssentials\/documentation\/FoundationEssentials\/ParseStrategy"},{"text":" exist in the ","type":"text"},{"code":"FoundationInternationalization","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" module.","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"FoundationInternationalization"},{"type":"text","text":" also extends types in both "},{"code":"FoundationEssentials","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and the Swift Standard Library to add formatting and parsing support.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"When you import ","type":"text"},{"code":"FoundationInternationalization","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", you have two general approaches to perform formatting of supported types:","type":"text"}]},{"items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Call "},{"code":"formatted()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" or "},{"code":"formatted(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" on an instance of the type, optionally passing in a customized "},{"code":"FormatStyle","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" appropriate to the type. These methods, defined by extensions in "},{"code":"FoundationInternationalization","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", are useful for performing one-off formatting with default styles or slightly-customized styles. For example, "},{"code":"var string123 = Double(1.23).formatted()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" creates the string "},{"code":"1.23","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"typ